# A string operator written as a method suggests the operator (M1-19).
mode: syntax
---- query
T | where name.contains("x")
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..29
  PIPELINE@0..28
    NAME_REF@0..1
      IDENT@0..1 "T"
    WHITESPACE@1..2 " "
    PIPE@2..3 "|"
    WHITESPACE@3..4 " "
    WHERE_OP@4..28
      IDENT@4..9 "where"
      WHITESPACE@9..10 " "
      CALL_EXPR@10..28
        FIELD_EXPR@10..23
          NAME_REF@10..14
            IDENT@10..14 "name"
          DOT@14..15 "."
          NAME_REF@15..23
            IDENT@15..23 "contains"
        ARG_LIST@23..28
          L_PAREN@23..24 "("
          LITERAL@24..27
            STRING@24..27 "\"x\""
          R_PAREN@27..28 ")"
  WHITESPACE@28..29 "\n"

error[DS0113]: DataScript has no method calls
  --> query:1:15
  |
1 | T | where name.contains("x")
  |               ^^^^^^^^^^ `contains` is called like a method of `name`
  |
  = help: `contains` is an operator that goes between two values: `name contains "x"`
